Workaround I used to take action after `requestBackgroundPermissionsAsync` is finished, for anyone interested

```
Location.requestBackgroundPermissionsAsync().then(() => {
  if (res.status === 'granted') {
    // permissions already enabled
  }
  if (AppState.currentState === 'active') {
    // permissions already disabled
  }
  // We are now asking the user for background permission, so the app will not be active
  // Once it is active again, get the updated permissions
  AppState.addEventListener('change', (state) => {
    if (state === 'active') {
      Location.getBackgroundPermissionsAsync().then((res) => {
        if (res.status === 'granted') {
          somefunction();
        }
      });
    }
  });
});
```

