I'll try the function proposed with checking the permission after the app comes back to foreground.

I made some changes on that workaround and now it works.
You have to make sure to ask for Foreground BEFORE, and then the background.

This code is working on [getnofilter.com](getnofilter.com) right now, in production

I am mixing promises with awaits, but it's just because I plan to remove the `.then` hack as soon as it gets solved.

```ts
      // Get Foreground location permission
      const forePermi = await Location.requestForegroundPermissionsAsync();
      if (!forePermi.granted) {
        Alert.alert('👀', i18n.t('We need your permission to check your location'));
        return;
      }

      // Get Background location permission
      const backPermi = await Location.requestBackgroundPermissionsAsync().then(res => {
        if (res.status === 'granted') {
          // permissions already enabled
          return res;
        }
        if (AppState.currentState === 'active') {
          // permissions already disabled
          return res;
        }

        return new Promise(resolve => {
          // We are now asking the user for background permission, so the app will not be active
          // Once it is active again, get the updated permissions
          const subs = AppState.addEventListener('change', state => {
            if (state === 'active') {
              Location.getBackgroundPermissionsAsync().then(newRes => {
                resolve(newRes);
              });

              subs.remove();
            }
          });
        });
      });
      if (!backPermi.granted) {
        Alert.alert('👀', i18n.t('We need your permission to check your location'));
        return;
      }
```

