> has this been released? i'm on `"expo": "^52.0.0",` and seeing this issue, still. it breaks our location permission request flow. even if the permission is granted by the user the `await Location.requestBackgroundPermissionsAsync()` returns `denied` status. doesn't seem fixed

I had a permissions request flow like this:
```
let location = await Location.requestForegroundPermissionsAsync();
if (location.status == "granted") {
  let background_location = await Location.requestBackgroundPermissionsAsync();
}
```
but when I called for background permission it always returned "denied", so I noticed that during all my sequence permissions prompts my appstate remained "inactive" and that expo started to read my foreground permission as "granted" only after all prompts where dismissed and appstate returned active. I suddendly understood that my `Location.requestBackgroundPermissionsAsync()` was automatically denied cause of this, and I realised I had to request for foreground permission, wait for the state of app to be "active" and only after ask for background permission. I implemented it like this:
```
let location = await Location.requestForegroundPermissionsAsync();
if (location.status == "granted") {
  await new Promise((resolve,reject)=>{
    AppState.addEventListener("change",(state)=>{
      const fallback = setTimeout(reject,2000) // if the app takes more than 2 seconds to get back "active", go ahead anyway
      if ( state== "active") {
        clearTimeout(fallback)
        resolve(null)
      }
    }
  )})
  let background_location = await Location.requestBackgroundPermissionsAsync();
}
```
hope it helps :)
